<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Baselines</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Group-Based Policy Optimization</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Group-based policy optimization methods update the policy by grouping multiple rollouts from the same problem and computing advantages relative to the group baseline.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GRPO.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite> computes advantages by comparing each solution’s reward to the mean reward of all solutions sampled from the same problem. For a problem <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with rollouts <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{x}=\{y^{(1)},\ldots,y^{(m)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{x}=\{y^{(1)},\ldots,y^{(m)}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and corresponding rewards <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R(y^{(j)}|x)\}_{j=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R(y^{(j)}|x)\}_{j=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, the advantage for solution <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\text{GRPO}}(y^{(i)}|x)=R(y^{(i)}|x)-\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}R(y^{(j)}|x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\text{GRPO}}(y^{(i)}|x)=R(y^{(i)}|x)-\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}R(y^{(j)}|x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The policy is then updated using a PPO-style clipped objective:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\text{GRPO}}(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{x,y^{(i)}\sim\mathcal{Y}_{x}}\left[\min\left(\rho_{i}A^{\text{GRPO}}(y^{(i)}|x),\text{clip}(\rho_{i},1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)A^{\text{GRPO}}(y^{(i)}|x)\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\text{GRPO}}(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{x,y^{(i)}\sim\mathcal{Y}_{x}}\left[\min\left(\rho_{i}A^{\text{GRPO}}(y^{(i)}|x),\text{clip}(\rho_{i},1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)A^{\text{GRPO}}(y^{(i)}|x)\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=\frac{\pi(y^{(i)}|x)}{\pi_{\text{old}}(y^{(i)}|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=\frac{\pi(y^{(i)}|x)}{\pi_{\text{old}}(y^{(i)}|x)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the importance ratio and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the clipping threshold.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GSPO.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Group-Sequence Policy Optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> addresses fundamental stability issues in GRPO by defining importance ratios at the sequence level rather than the token level. Unlike GRPO, which applies token-level importance weights that can introduce high-variance noise, GSPO computes importance ratios based on sequence likelihood, aligning with the principle of importance sampling.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">GSPO optimizes the following sequence-level objective:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{J}^{\text{GSPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot|x)}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\min\left(s_{i}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i},\text{clip}(s_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\hat{A}_{i}\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GSPO</mtext></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>clip</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}^{\text{GSPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot|x)}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\min\left(s_{i}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i},\text{clip}(s_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\hat{A}_{i}\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where the sequence-level importance ratio is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}(\theta)=\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i}|x)}\right)^{\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}}=\exp\left(\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}(\theta)=\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i}|x)}\right)^{\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}}=\exp\left(\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The advantage computation remains the same as in GRPO.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Mean Absolute Advantage as Curriculum Reward</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An ideal curriculum should prioritize training problems that maximize the model’s immediate learning outcomes. A natural way to quantify learning outcomes is through the magnitude of parameter updates induced by the selected training data, which can be approximated by the absolute advantage.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the common setting of RL with verifiable binary rewards, mean absolute advantage has a attractive interpretation. When using group-based RL methods like GRPO with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> rollouts per problem, the advantage for the <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th rollout is computed as:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{t,i}=\frac{r_{i}-\text{mean}(r)}{\text{std}(r)}=\frac{r_{i}-p}{\sqrt{p(1-p)}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>std</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{t,i}=\frac{r_{i}-\text{mean}(r)}{\text{std}(r)}=\frac{r_{i}-p}{\sqrt{p(1-p)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is the empirical success rate over the group. Since the reward <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a Bernoulli distribution, the expected absolute advantage is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\hat{A}_{t,i}|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\hat{A}_{t,i}|]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p\cdot\frac{1-p}{\sqrt{p(1-p)}}+(1-p)\cdot\frac{p}{\sqrt{p(1-p)}}=2\sqrt{p(1-p)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p\cdot\frac{1-p}{\sqrt{p(1-p)}}+(1-p)\cdot\frac{p}{\sqrt{p(1-p)}}=2\sqrt{p(1-p)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The function <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(p)=2\sqrt{p(1-p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(p)=2\sqrt{p(1-p)}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric around <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, strictly concave on <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and reaches its maximum at <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, maximizing expected absolute advantage is equivalent to prioritizing problems at a success rate of 50%.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Value-Based Curation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Value-based curation methods maintain explicit estimates of the utility or learning value associated with training data, which are then used to guide adaptive curriculum selection during RL post-training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The core principle of value-based curation is to learn a utility function <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that maps training data to expected learning outcomes at training step <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the space over which utilities are estimated (e.g., individual problems, problem categories, or problem features). The utility function <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> assigns a scalar value to each element <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">During curriculum selection, the curator samples from <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> according to a policy derived from <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. A common choice is the Boltzmann (softmax) policy:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(s)=\frac{\exp(Q_{t}(s)/\eta)}{\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}\exp(Q_{t}(s^{\prime})/\eta)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(s)=\frac{\exp(Q_{t}(s)/\eta)}{\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}\exp(Q_{t}(s^{\prime})/\eta)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a temperature parameter that controls the exploration-exploitation tradeoff: higher temperatures lead to more uniform sampling (exploration), while lower temperatures concentrate probability mass on high-utility items (exploitation).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The utility function is updated over time based on observed learning outcomes. After selecting data according to <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and performing an RL update, the curator observes a reward signal <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> that measures the actual learning value obtained. These observations are used to refine <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SEC.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Self-Evolving Curriculum (SEC) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> instantiates value-based curation by defining the utility space <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=C</annotation></semantics></math> as a discrete set of problem categories (e.g., difficulty levels, problem types). The utility function <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}:C\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}:C\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is represented as a lookup table, with one scalar value per category.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">SEC uses temporal difference (TD) learning to update utilities:</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t+1}(c)=\alpha r_{t}(c)+(1-\alpha)Q_{t}(c)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t+1}(c)=\alpha r_{t}(c)+(1-\alpha)Q_{t}(c),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is a learning rate and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}(c)</annotation></semantics></math> is the mean absolute advantage aggregated over all problems from category <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> selected at step <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. This exponential moving average naturally adapts to non-stationarity as category utilities change with model improvement.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Curriculum selection proceeds in two stages: first, a category is sampled according to the Boltzmann policy <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(c)\propto\exp(Q_{t}(c)/\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(c)\propto\exp(Q_{t}(c)/\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>; then, problems are uniformly sampled from the selected category.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regression.</span>
An alternative instantiation defines the utility space <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> directly at the problem level, estimating utilities for individual training problems. The utility function is parameterized by a neural network <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\phi}:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\phi}:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that takes problem representations (e.g., text embeddings) as input.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Rather than incremental TD updates, the curator is trained via supervised regression. Let <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{t}=\{(x_{j},r_{j})\}_{j=1}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{t}=\{(x_{j},r_{j})\}_{j=1}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the history of problem-reward observations. The utility network is optimized to minimize mean squared error:</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{MSE}}(\phi)=\sum_{(x_{j},r_{j})\in\mathcal{H}_{t}}\left(Q_{\phi}(x_{j})-r_{j}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>MSE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{MSE}}(\phi)=\sum_{(x_{j},r_{j})\in\mathcal{H}_{t}}\left(Q_{\phi}(x_{j})-r_{j}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This can be optimized periodically (every <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> steps) via batch gradient descent, or online via stochastic gradient descent:</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t+1}=\phi_{t}-\beta\nabla_{\phi}\left(Q_{\phi}(x_{t})-r_{t}(x_{t})\right)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t+1}=\phi_{t}-\beta\nabla_{\phi}\left(Q_{\phi}(x_{t})-r_{t}(x_{t})\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate. Problems are sampled directly according to <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)\propto\exp(Q_{\phi}(x)/\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)\propto\exp(Q_{\phi}(x)/\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PCL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2025</a>)</cite> exemplifies the online regression approach. PCL updates <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> concurrently with policy training using only the current batch of observations. At each step <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, PCL samples a candidate pool of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="km" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">km</annotation></semantics></math> prompts and selects the <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> prompts whose predicted values are closest to a target threshold <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> (typically 0.5):</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{m}=\arg\min_{S\subseteq D_{km},|S|=m}\sum_{x\in S}|Q_{\phi}(x)-\tau|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{m}=\arg\min_{S\subseteq D_{km},|S|=m}\sum_{x\in S}|Q_{\phi}(x)-\tau|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">This greedy selection can be viewed as an extreme limit of Boltzmann sampling with a sharply peaked distribution. Consider the modified utility <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Q}(x)=-|Q_{\phi}(x)-\tau|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Q}(x)=-|Q_{\phi}(x)-\tau|</annotation></semantics></math>, which measures negative distance from the threshold. As the temperature <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the Boltzmann policy <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)\propto\exp(\tilde{Q}(x)/\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)\propto\exp(\tilde{Q}(x)/\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates all probability mass on prompts nearest to <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, recovering PCL’s greedy selection. This deterministic selection strategy is computationally efficient and ensures the training batch contains only prompts of target difficulty, maximizing the effective ratio of informative gradient signals.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">After selecting prompts, PCL generates <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> responses per prompt and updates both the policy and value model. The value model is trained on the observed rewards from the selected prompts:</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{PCL}}(\phi)=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(Q_{\phi}(x_{i})-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(x_{i},y_{i,j})\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>PCL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{PCL}}(\phi)=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(Q_{\phi}(x_{i})-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(x_{i},y_{i,j})\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Comparison to Actor-Curator.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Actor-Curator framework with OSMD differs fundamentally from value-based curation methods in its optimization objective and data selection mechanism. While value-based methods learn utilities <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> to predict expected learning outcomes and sample accordingly, OSMD directly optimizes a curriculum distribution <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to maximize expected policy improvement. Value-based approaches require estimating problem-level or category-level values and making selection decisions based on these estimates—a two-stage process that introduces approximation error. In contrast, OSMD treats curriculum optimization as a first-order problem: the gradient <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{q}J(\pi_{t},\boldsymbol{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>q</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{q}J(\pi_{t},\boldsymbol{p})</annotation></semantics></math> directly specifies how to adjust the data distribution to improve the policy, without requiring intermediate value estimates. Furthermore, value-based methods typically rely on scalar reward signals <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> to update utilities, whereas OSMD leverages the full gradient information <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\pi_{t};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\pi_{t};x)</annotation></semantics></math> to measure the learning value of each problem. This allows OSMD to capture richer information about how individual problems affect policy optimization, beyond what a single scalar reward can convey.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Policy improvement estimation</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section proves unbiasedness of the per-problem bandit feedback estimators used to train the curator.
Recall the per-problem utility at iteration <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Eq. 6 ‣ Per-problem utility. ‣ 3.2 Policy improvement as the curator learning signal ‣ 3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{\boldsymbol{x}}^{t}=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\EE_{\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})}\left[\frac{\pi^{t+1}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}{\pi^{t}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}A_{\pi^{t}}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.059em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\boldsymbol{x}}^{t}=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\EE_{\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})}\left[\frac{\pi^{t+1}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}{\pi^{t}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}A_{\pi^{t}}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We also recall the rollout-based estimator (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E7" title="Eq. 7 ‣ Utility estimation and OSMD bandit feedback. ‣ 3.3 Tabular OSMD formulation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\triangleq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Y}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}|}\sum_{\boldsymbol{y}\in\mathcal{Y}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}}\frac{\pi^{t+1}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}{\pi^{t}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}A_{\pi^{t}}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x}),\quad\mathcal{Y}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}=\{\boldsymbol{y}^{(j)}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\}_{j=1}^{|\mathcal{Y}_{\boldsymbol{x}}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\triangleq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Y}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}|}\sum_{\boldsymbol{y}\in\mathcal{Y}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}}\frac{\pi^{t+1}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}{\pi^{t}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}A_{\pi^{t}}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x}),\quad\mathcal{Y}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}=\{\boldsymbol{y}^{(j)}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\}_{j=1}^{|\mathcal{Y}_{\boldsymbol{x}}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Single-stage case</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Unbiasedness (single-stage))</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the estimator in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E7" title="Eq. 7 ‣ Utility estimation and OSMD bandit feedback. ‣ 3.3 Tabular OSMD formulation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}}{p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x})}\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}}{p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x})}\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">we have <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EE[\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}]=u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">u</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}]=u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix an iteration <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and a problem <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the single-stage setting, the training set <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled directly from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>
according to the curator distribution <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{t}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{t}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t})=p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t})=p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is an unbiased estimator of the population quantity</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE_{\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})}\left[\frac{\pi^{t+1}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}{\pi^{t}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}A_{\pi^{t}}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE_{\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})}\left[\frac{\pi^{t+1}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}{\pi^{t}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}A_{\pi^{t}}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">by i.i.d. rollout sampling and linearity of expectation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, take expectation of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioning on <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE\!\left[\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}\mid\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\EE\!\left[\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}}{p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right]\,\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>𝔼</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.059em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>𝔼</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\!\left[\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}\mid\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\EE\!\left[\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}}{p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right]\,\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE[\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}]=\Pr(\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t})=p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}]=\Pr(\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t})=p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, taking expectation over rollout randomness yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE[\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\EE\!\left[\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.059em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>𝔼</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\hat{U}^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\EE\!\left[\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which proves the claim.
 <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Two-stage case</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Unbiasedness (two-stage))</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the two-stage estimator in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Eq. 10 ‣ Utility estimation. ‣ 3.5 Two-stage sampling ‣ 3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}}{q(\boldsymbol{x})\,p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})}\;\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>two</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}}{q(\boldsymbol{x})\,p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})}\;\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">we have <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EE[\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}]=u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>two</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">u</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}]=u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix an iteration <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and a problem <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition of the two-stage procedure (Section <a href="#S3.SS5" title="3.5 Two-stage sampling ‣ 3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>),
the candidate set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, inducing the marginal inclusion probability
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\boldsymbol{x})=\Pr(\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\boldsymbol{x})=\Pr(\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Conditioned on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the curator selects the training set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}^{t}\subset\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}^{t}\subset\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
according to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{t}(\cdot\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{t}(\cdot\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As in the single-stage case, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is an unbiased estimator of the corresponding population
expectation under <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now condition on the realized candidate set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\notin\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\notin\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}=0</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.
If <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, then by the selection step,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE\!\left[\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\right]=p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>𝔼</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\!\left[\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\right]=p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE\!\left[\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}}{p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})}\;\middle|\;\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t},\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>𝔼</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\!\left[\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}\}}{p^{t}(\boldsymbol{x}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})}\;\middle|\;\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t},\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting into the estimator gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE\!\left[\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}\;\middle|\;\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t},\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\}}{q(\boldsymbol{x})}\;\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>𝔼</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>two</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\!\left[\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}\;\middle|\;\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t},\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\frac{\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\}}{q(\boldsymbol{x})}\;\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Taking expectation over the proposal step yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE\!\left[\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}\;\middle|\;\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\frac{\EE[\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\}]}{q(\boldsymbol{x})}\;\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>𝔼</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>two</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\!\left[\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}\;\middle|\;\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\frac{\EE[\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\}]}{q(\boldsymbol{x})}\;\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE[\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\}]=\Pr(\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})=q(\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\mathbb{I}\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t}\}]=\Pr(\boldsymbol{x}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}^{t})=q(\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, taking expectation over rollout randomness gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE[\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\EE[\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})]=u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>two</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.059em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\hat{U}^{t}_{\mathrm{two},\boldsymbol{x}}]=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\EE[\hat{A}^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})]=u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.6" class="ltx_p">which proves the claim.
 <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Idealized OSMD algorithm</h2>

<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Sleeping Online Mirror Descent</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          Number of total arms <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, number of available arms <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> each round, horizon <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, step size <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, exploration parameter <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1/k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1/k)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Initialize <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}_{1}=(1/K,\dots,1/K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}_{1}=(1/K,\dots,1/K)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            Sample available subset <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Compute

<table id="A3.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})=\begin{cases}\frac{\boldsymbol{p}_{t,i}}{\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{p}_{t,j}}&amp;\text{if $i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}$}\\
0\quad&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})=\begin{cases}\frac{\boldsymbol{p}_{t,i}}{\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{p}_{t,j}}&amp;\text{if $i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}$}\\
0\quad&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            Sample <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{t,1},a_{t,2},\dots,a_{t,s}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle i.i.d.}}{{\sim}}\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(\cdot\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mover><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t,1},a_{t,2},\dots,a_{t,s}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle i.i.d.}}{{\sim}}\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(\cdot\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Loss Estimator)</span> For each arm <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, set

<table id="A3.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E26X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{L}_{t,i}=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\mathbf{1}\{a_{t,r}=i\}\frac{l_{t,i}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{L}_{t,i}=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\mathbf{1}\{a_{t,r}=i\}\frac{l_{t,i}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(OSMD Update)</span> Update the next distribution by the mirror step

<table id="A3.E27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E27X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{p}_{t+1}\in\arg\min_{p\in\mathcal{A}}\left\{\eta\,\langle p,\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}\rangle+D_{F}(p,\boldsymbol{p}_{t})\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{p}_{t+1}\in\arg\min_{p\in\mathcal{A}}\left\{\eta\,\langle p,\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}\rangle+D_{F}(p,\boldsymbol{p}_{t})\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E27Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{where}\quad D_{F}(\boldsymbol{u},\boldsymbol{v})=\sum_{i}u_{i}\log\frac{u_{i}}{v_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{where}\quad D_{F}(\boldsymbol{u},\boldsymbol{v})=\sum_{i}u_{i}\log\frac{u_{i}}{v_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Setup</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We formalize the tabular bandit algorithm in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> as Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Under this idealized algorithm. We assume there is a large set of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> arms. At each time step <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> arms are uniformly randomly chosen as candidate arms. The settings allows for the pulling of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> arms per round, and after each round the loss <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> is revealed for each chosen arm <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the arm’s original index in <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[K]</annotation></semantics></math>. Throughout this section and the next, we denote the vectorized quantities with bold font. For example <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{l}_{t}=(l_{t,1},\dots,l_{t,K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{l}_{t}=(l_{t,1},\dots,l_{t,K})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> departs from traditional Online Stochastic Mirror Descent (OSMD) due to the availability constraint. The action distribution is conditioned on a randomly sampled <em id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">available set</em> at each round, and the loss estimator is modified to remain unbiased under this conditional sampling.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Eqn. (<a href="#A3.E25" title="Eq. 25In Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) introduces a two-stage sampling process. First, a random <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-subset <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\subseteq[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\subseteq[K]</annotation></semantics></math> of available arms is drawn uniformly. The learner then constructs a <em id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">conditional distribution</em></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})=\frac{\boldsymbol{p}_{t,i}}{\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{p}_{t,j}}\quad\text{for }i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})=\frac{\boldsymbol{p}_{t,i}}{\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{p}_{t,j}}\quad\text{for }i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and assigns zero probability to arms outside <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We sometimes also use <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> to denote <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. This renormalization ensures that the learner only samples from arms that are available at round <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, while still using <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the global state variable that is updated over time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The conditional sampling in Eqn. (<a href="#A3.E25" title="Eq. 25In Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) invalidates the standard OSMD estimator, since <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> is no longer the actual probability with which arm <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled. Eqn. (<a href="#A3.E26" title="Eq. 26In Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) addresses this by defining</p>
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{L}_{t,i}=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\mathbf{1}\{a_{t,r}=i\}\frac{l_{t,i}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{L}_{t,i}=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\mathbf{1}\{a_{t,r}=i\}\frac{l_{t,i}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This estimator uses the conditional probability <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> in the denominator, which is the true sampling probability of arm <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> given the realized availability set. As a result, conditional on <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the estimator is unbiased:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\widehat{L}_{t,i}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=l_{t,i}\,\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\widehat{L}_{t,i}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=l_{t,i}\,\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">The use of <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> independent samples further reduces variance and corresponds to a semi-bandit feedback model, but does not change the role of the estimator in the mirror update.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Regret Analysis</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section presents a proof of the regret bound (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 ‣ Regret guarantee. ‣ 3.5 Two-stage sampling ‣ 3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) for Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Suppose there are <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> base arms <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[K]=\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[K]=\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> each corresponding to a problem in the dataset <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}=\{\boldsymbol{x}^{(1)},\boldsymbol{x}^{(2)},\dots,\boldsymbol{x}^{(K)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}=\{\boldsymbol{x}^{(1)},\boldsymbol{x}^{(2)},\dots,\boldsymbol{x}^{(K)}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. At each step, a subset <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn uniformly randomly from <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every round <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, The curator picks <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> arms <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t,1},a_{t,2},\dots,a_{t,s}\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t,1},a_{t,2},\dots,a_{t,s}\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the loss for each arm <math id="A4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{t,a_{t,i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{t,a_{t,i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is revealed. For convenience, write <math id="A4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{l}_{t}=(l_{t,1},\dots,l_{t,K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{l}_{t}=(l_{t,1},\dots,l_{t,K})</annotation></semantics></math> to be the losses of each arm as a vector. Assume without loss of generality that <math id="A4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{t,i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{t,i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the subset-masked loss vector <math id="A4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)=\begin{cases}\boldsymbol{l}_{t}(i)&amp;\text{if }i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)=\begin{cases}\boldsymbol{l}_{t}(i)&amp;\text{if }i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Denote the best available arm at time <math id="A4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A4.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}=\arg\min_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}l_{t,i}\text{ and }l^{*}_{t}=l_{t,m_{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=\arg\min_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}l_{t,i}\text{ and }l^{*}_{t}=l_{t,m_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We define the <span id="A4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">best-arm regret</span> to be</p>
<table id="A4.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Reg}_{T}^{\mathrm{best}}=\EE\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}(\sum_{i=1}^{s}l_{t,a_{t,s}}-l^{*}_{t})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Reg</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>best</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Reg}_{T}^{\mathrm{best}}=\EE\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}(\sum_{i=1}^{s}l_{t,a_{t,s}}-l^{*}_{t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Note that the regret can be expressed in the vectorized form.</p>
<table id="A4.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Reg}_{n}^{\mathrm{best}}=\EE\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{e}_{m_{t}},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>best</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Reg}_{n}^{\mathrm{best}}=\EE\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{e}_{m_{t}},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{e}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{e}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a one-hot vector with <math id="A4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> on index <math id="A4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, we use <math id="A4.p1.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> to represent the vector <math id="A4.p1.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{x}^{(1)}),\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{x}^{(2)}),\dots,\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{x}^{(K)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{x}^{(1)}),\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{x}^{(2)}),\dots,\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{x}^{(K)}))</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, forcing uniform exploration usually have negligible or even positive effect on the performance. However, it incurs linear regret for theoretical analysis. Thus, to focus on how OSMD manages losses in a non-stationary environment, this regret analysis isolate the loss attributable to factors other than uniform exploration. Towards this end, we set the comparator <math id="A4.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a mixture of the best available arm and uniform distribution over all arms.</p>
<table id="A4.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{q}_{t}=(1-k\alpha)\boldsymbol{e}_{m_{t}}+\alpha\boldsymbol{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{q}_{t}=(1-k\alpha)\boldsymbol{e}_{m_{t}}+\alpha\boldsymbol{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is a binary vector with <math id="A4.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and zero everywhere else. The <span id="A4.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">best-available regret</span> is defined as</p>
<table id="A4.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Reg}_{T}^{\mathrm{BA}}=\EE\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Reg</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>BA</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Reg}_{T}^{\mathrm{BA}}=\EE\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Restatement of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 ‣ Regret guarantee. ‣ 3.5 Two-stage sampling ‣ 3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the drift parameter</span></p>
<table id="A4.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{T}=\sum_{t=2}^{T}\Delta_{t},\quad\Delta_{t}=\max_{i\in[K]}\left|l_{t,i}-l_{t-1,i}\right|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{T}=\sum_{t=2}^{T}\Delta_{t},\quad\Delta_{t}=\max_{i\in[K]}\left|l_{t,i}-l_{t-1,i}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">be a measure of how rapid the arm values changes over time <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume without loss of generality that <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{l}_{t,i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{l}_{t,i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Reg}^{\mathrm{BA}}_{n}\leq O\left(T^{2/3}V_{n}^{1/3}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>BA</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Reg}^{\mathrm{BA}}_{n}\leq O\left(T^{2/3}V_{n}^{1/3}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To bound the smoothed regret, the proof follows a block decomposition argument. We partition the horizon into contiguous blocks of length <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and restart the algorithm at the beginning of each block. Within a single block, the loss sequence is treated as approximately stationary, allowing us to compare the algorithm against a fixed comparator using standard OSMD analysis. The regret within each block is controlled by a stability–variance tradeoff: the mirror descent inequality yields a term of order <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log(1/\alpha)/\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log(1/\alpha)/\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>, while the variance of the importance-weighted estimator contributes a term proportional to <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\eta B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\eta B)</annotation></semantics></math>. Across blocks, non-stationarity is captured through a variation budget <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which upper bounds the cumulative discrepancy between the true per-round losses and the frozen losses used in the blockwise analysis, contributing an additive term of order <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BV_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BV_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The block length <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is then optimized to balance the statistical cost of restarting too frequently against the bias induced by treating losses as stationary within each block. This optimization yields a regret bound scaling as <math id="A4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(V_{n}^{1/3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(V_{n}^{1/3})</annotation></semantics></math>, reflecting the classical tradeoff between adaptivity to non-stationarity and estimation error <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Besbes et al. (2014)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let the length of each aforementioned block be <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote the start time of each block as <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{l}=(l-1)L+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{l}=(l-1)L+1</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,2,\dots,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,2,\dots,B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=T/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=T/L</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          For convenience, we assume <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is divisible by B and L at the same time.</span></span></span>. Denote the time steps of the <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th block as <math id="A4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{l}=\{\tau_{l},\dots,\tau_{l}+L-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{l}=\{\tau_{l},\dots,\tau_{l}+L-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A4.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Reg}_{n}^{\mathrm{BA}}=\EE\left[\sum_{t=1}^{n}\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\right]=\sum_{l=1}^{B}\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}_{l}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}},\boldsymbol{y}_{t}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>BA</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Reg}_{n}^{\mathrm{BA}}=\EE\left[\sum_{t=1}^{n}\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\right]=\sum_{l=1}^{B}\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}_{l}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}},\boldsymbol{y}_{t}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Time-Frozen Comparator</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This part of the proof introduces a stable reference for comparison in the presence of non-stationary losses. Rather than comparing the learner to the best action at every round, which may change arbitrarily over time, we define a comparator based on the losses at a fixed reference <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. This “time-frozen” comparator serves as a proxy for the per-round best action. The construction allows us to relate the learner’s loss to this frozen benchmark, while the error incurred by freezing time can be bounded by the amount of variation in the losses.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}^{\tau}\in\arg\min_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}y_{\tau,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}^{\tau}\in\arg\min_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}y_{\tau,i}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-frozen best arm of time <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote the value associated with this arm <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}=y_{\tau,m_{t}^{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}=y_{\tau,m_{t}^{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we can define the time-frozen smooth comparator</p>
<table id="A4.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau}=(1-k\alpha)\boldsymbol{e}_{m_{t}^{\tau}}+\alpha\boldsymbol{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau}=(1-k\alpha)\boldsymbol{e}_{m_{t}^{\tau}}+\alpha\boldsymbol{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}=\{\tau,\dots,\tau+L-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}=\{\tau,\dots,\tau+L-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary block. Suppose <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be as defined in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Restatement of Theorem ) ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. For any sequence of random variables <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{t}\}_{t\in\mathcal{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{t}\}_{t\in\mathcal{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> with a common support, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}X_{t}-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right]\leq\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}X_{t}-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}^{\tau}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right]+\frac{1-k\alpha}{k\alpha}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}\|\boldsymbol{l}_{t}-\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}\|_{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}X_{t}-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right]\leq\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}X_{t}-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}^{\tau}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right]+\frac{1-k\alpha}{k\alpha}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}\|\boldsymbol{l}_{t}-\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By the definition of <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.E39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E39X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau},\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>τ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau},\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1-k\alpha)(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}+\alpha\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1-k\alpha)(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}+\alpha\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E39Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1-k\alpha(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}+\alpha(k(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}+k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1-k\alpha(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}+\alpha(k(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}+k-1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E39Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=m_{t}^{\tau}+\alpha(k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=m_{t}^{\tau}+\alpha(k-1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Rearranging (<a href="#A4.E39" title="Eq. 39 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.1 Time-Frozen Comparator ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) and divide by <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A4.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{m_{t}^{\tau}}{Z_{t}}\geq\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle-\frac{\alpha(k-1)}{Z_{t}}\geq\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle-\frac{k-1}{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>τ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>τ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{m_{t}^{\tau}}{Z_{t}}\geq\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle-\frac{\alpha(k-1)}{Z_{t}}\geq\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}^{\tau},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle-\frac{k-1}{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using the fact that <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>min</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min</annotation></semantics></math> is a Lipschitz operation, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|y^{*}_{t}-(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}\right|=\left|\min_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{l}_{t,i}-\min_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau,i}\right|\leq\|\boldsymbol{l}_{t}-\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}\|_{\infty}\leq\|\boldsymbol{l}_{t}-\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}\|_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|y^{*}_{t}-(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}\right|=\left|\min_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{l}_{t,i}-\min_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau,i}\right|\leq\|\boldsymbol{l}_{t}-\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}\|_{\infty}\leq\|\boldsymbol{l}_{t}-\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}\|_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Applying this identity, we have</p>
<table id="A4.E41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E41X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}^{\tau}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}^{\tau}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{k\alpha}\left|\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}^{\tau}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{k\alpha}\left|\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}^{\tau}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E41Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1-k\alpha}{k\alpha}\left|y^{*}_{t}-(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1-k\alpha}{k\alpha}\left|y^{*}_{t}-(y^{*}_{t})^{\tau}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E41Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1-k\alpha}{k\alpha}\|\mathbf{y}_{t}-\mathbf{y}_{\tau}\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1-k\alpha}{k\alpha}\|\mathbf{y}_{t}-\mathbf{y}_{\tau}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Rearrange (<a href="#A4.E41" title="Eq. 41 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.1 Time-Frozen Comparator ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) and add <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to both sides while taking expectation, we get</p>
<table id="A4.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}X_{t}-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right]\leq\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}X_{t}-\left\langle\mathbf{q}^{\tau}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right]+\frac{1-k\alpha}{k\alpha}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}\|\boldsymbol{l}_{t}-\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}\|_{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}X_{t}-\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right]\leq\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}X_{t}-\left\langle\mathbf{q}^{\tau}_{t},\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}}{Z_{t}}\right\rangle\right]+\frac{1-k\alpha}{k\alpha}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{I}}\|\boldsymbol{l}_{t}-\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Moment Lemmas</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To apply the standard OMD bound (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Restatement of Theorem ) ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), we require unbiased loss estimates with controlled variance. Since the learner only observes losses on the sampled subset (<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), we work with an importance-weighted estimator that accounts for both subset sampling and the normalization induced by <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following two lemmas establish the properties needed for the regret analysis. The first shows that the estimator is unbiased for the scaled loss, ensuring that the expected update direction matches the true loss. The second provides a bound on the second moment of the estimator, which controls the variance term in the OSMD regret bound. Together, these results justify the use of the estimator in the mirror descent analysis and quantify the cost introduced by partial observation and uniform exploration.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Unbiasedness)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{L}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{L}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> be as defined in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Denote <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}=(\widehat{L}_{t,1},\widehat{L}_{t,2},\dots,\widehat{L}_{t,K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}=(\widehat{L}_{t,1},\widehat{L}_{t,2},\dots,\widehat{L}_{t,K})</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE[\widehat{L}_{t,i}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}]=\boldsymbol{l}_{t,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}=\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)\\
" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\widehat{L}_{t,i}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}]=\boldsymbol{l}_{t,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}=\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)\\
</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Additionally, define the time-frozen estimator</span></p>
<table id="A4.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{\tau}:=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\mathbb{I}\{a_{t,r}=i\}\frac{l_{\tau,i}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{\tau}:=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\mathbb{I}\{a_{t,r}=i\}\frac{l_{\tau,i}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE[\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{\tau}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}]=l_{\tau,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}=\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>τ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{\tau}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}]=l_{\tau,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}=\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}(i)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE\left[\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{\tau}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\boldsymbol{p}_{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})\frac{l_{t,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}=l_{t,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\left[\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{\tau}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\boldsymbol{p}_{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})\frac{l_{t,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}=l_{t,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE\left[\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{\tau}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\boldsymbol{p}_{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})\frac{l_{\tau,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}=l_{\tau,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\left[\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{\tau}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}\boldsymbol{p}_{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})\frac{l_{\tau,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}=l_{\tau,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Bounded Second Moment)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{L}_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{L}_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math> be as defined in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Suppose we obtain <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> through</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}^{t}\in\arg\min_{\boldsymbol{p}\in\mathcal{A}}\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{p},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}\right\rangle+D_{F}(\boldsymbol{p},\boldsymbol{p}^{t-1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}^{t}\in\arg\min_{\boldsymbol{p}\in\mathcal{A}}\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{p},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}\right\rangle+D_{F}(\boldsymbol{p},\boldsymbol{p}^{t-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">under the constraint <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i)\geq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i)\geq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="A4.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EE\left[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{j}\widehat{L}_{t,j}^{2}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]\leq\frac{k}{s}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\left[\sum_{j=1}^{K}\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{j}\widehat{L}_{t,j}^{2}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]\leq\frac{k}{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\not\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\not\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{L}_{t,j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{L}_{t,j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, For <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="A4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r,j}:=\mathbb{I}\left\{A_{t,r=j}\right\}\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau,j}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})},\quad\text{consequently }\widehat{L}_{t,j}=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}X_{r,j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>consequently </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r,j}:=\mathbb{I}\left\{A_{t,r=j}\right\}\frac{\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau,j}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})},\quad\text{consequently }\widehat{L}_{t,j}=\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}X_{r,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By construction, <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r,j}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are IID in <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, and since <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau,j}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{l}_{\tau,j}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EE\left[X^{2}_{r,j}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})\frac{\boldsymbol{l}^{2}_{\tau,j}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})^{2}}\leq\frac{1}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\left[X^{2}_{r,j}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})\frac{\boldsymbol{l}^{2}_{\tau,j}}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})^{2}}\leq\frac{1}{\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By Jensen’s inequality, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE\left[(\widehat{L}_{t,j}^{\tau})^{2}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=\EE\left[\left(\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}X_{r,j}\right)^{2}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]\leq\frac{1}{s}\EE\left[X_{r,j}^{2}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]\leq\frac{1}{s\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\left[(\widehat{L}_{t,j}^{\tau})^{2}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]=\EE\left[\left(\frac{1}{s}\sum_{r=1}^{s}X_{r,j}\right)^{2}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]\leq\frac{1}{s}\EE\left[X_{r,j}^{2}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]\leq\frac{1}{s\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(j\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Summing with weights <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\left(\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right)_{j}\EE\left[(\widehat{L}_{t,j}^{\tau})^{2}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]\leq\frac{1}{s}\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\left(\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right)_{j}\frac{Z_{t}}{\left(\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right)_{j}}=\frac{k}{s}Z_{t}\leq\frac{k}{s}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mfrac><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐩</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\left(\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right)_{j}\EE\left[(\widehat{L}_{t,j}^{\tau})^{2}\middle|\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\right]\leq\frac{1}{s}\sum_{j\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\left(\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right)_{j}\frac{Z_{t}}{\left(\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right)_{j}}=\frac{k}{s}Z_{t}\leq\frac{k}{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>One-Step OMD Bound</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The purpose of the following lemma is to provide a local inequality that governs how a single mirror descent update behaves under the importance-weighted loss estimator. When summed over time, the KL terms telescope while the second-moment terms accumulate in a controlled manner. This structure allows the proof to separate the effect of the update rule from issues caused by partial observability and non-stationarity, which are handled in later steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are obtained as in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Then, for any comparator <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\in\Delta_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\in\Delta_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}-\boldsymbol{v}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\leq\frac{1}{\eta}\left(\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{p}^{t+1}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t+1}})\right)+\frac{\eta s^{2}}{2}\sum_{i\in C_{t}}\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}-\boldsymbol{v}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle\leq\frac{1}{\eta}\left(\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{p}^{t+1}_{\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t+1}})\right)+\frac{\eta s^{2}}{2}\sum_{i\in C_{t}}\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the simplicity of the proof, fix <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=\boldsymbol{p}^{t}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\boldsymbol{p}^{t}(i\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{L}_{i}=\widehat{L}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{L}_{i}=\widehat{L}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Write the updated weights as <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{+}=p_{i}\exp(-\eta\widehat{L}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{+}=p_{i}\exp(-\eta\widehat{L}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and the updated active sum as <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{+}=\sum_{i\in C}p^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{+}=\sum_{i\in C}p^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{+}=p_{i}^{+}/Z^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{+}=p_{i}^{+}/Z^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the vector form of the aforementioned quantities in bold. e.g. <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{p}(i)=p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{p}(i)=p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note</p>
<table id="A4.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{q_{i}}{q_{i}^{+}}=\log\frac{p_{i}/Z}{p_{i}\exp(-\eta\widehat{L}_{i})/Z^{+}}=\log\frac{Z^{+}}{Z}+\eta\widehat{L}_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{q_{i}}{q_{i}^{+}}=\log\frac{p_{i}/Z}{p_{i}\exp(-\eta\widehat{L}_{i})/Z^{+}}=\log\frac{Z^{+}}{Z}+\eta\widehat{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now,</p>
<table id="A4.E49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E49X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q}^{+})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q}^{+})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in C}v_{i}\log\frac{v_{i}}{q^{+}_{i}}-\sum_{i\in C}v_{i}\log\frac{v_{i}}{q_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in C}v_{i}\log\frac{v_{i}}{q^{+}_{i}}-\sum_{i\in C}v_{i}\log\frac{v_{i}}{q_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E49Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in C}v_{i}\log\frac{q_{i}}{q^{+}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in C}v_{i}\log\frac{q_{i}}{q^{+}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E49Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{Z^{+}}{Z}+\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{v},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{Z^{+}}{Z}+\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{v},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Rearranging we have</p>
<table id="A4.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{v},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle=\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q}^{+})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q})-\log\frac{Z^{+}}{Z}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{v},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle=\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q}^{+})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q})-\log\frac{Z^{+}}{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Next, apply the fact that <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-x}\leq 1-x+x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-x}\leq 1-x+x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and taking logs, we have</p>
<table id="A4.E51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E51X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{Z^{+}}{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{Z^{+}}{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\left(\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\left(1-\eta\widehat{L}_{i}+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\left(\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\left(1-\eta\widehat{L}_{i}+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E51Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(1-\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{q},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(1-\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{q},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E51Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{q},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{q},\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where the last inequality applies <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+x)\leq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+x)\leq x</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now plug (<a href="#A4.E51" title="Eq. 51 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.3 One-Step OMD Bound ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) into (<a href="#A4.E50" title="Eq. 50 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.3 One-Step OMD Bound ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A4.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{v},\hat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle\geq\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q}^{+})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q})+\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{q},\hat{\boldsymbol{y}}\right\rangle+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{v},\hat{\boldsymbol{L}}\right\rangle\geq\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q}^{+})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q})+\eta\left\langle\boldsymbol{q},\hat{\boldsymbol{y}}\right\rangle+\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Rearranging the inequality and dividing by <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A4.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle\boldsymbol{q}-\boldsymbol{v},\mathbf{\widehat{L}}\rangle\leq\frac{1}{\eta}(\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q}))+\frac{\eta}{2}\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\boldsymbol{q}-\boldsymbol{v},\mathbf{\widehat{L}}\rangle\leq\frac{1}{\eta}(\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}\|\boldsymbol{q}))+\frac{\eta}{2}\sum_{i\in C}q_{i}\widehat{L}_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting the original notation back, we recover the claim.
 <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The next two lemmas connect the one-step bound to a blockwise analysis under non-stationarity. Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 ‣ D.4 Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> controls the discrepancy between the per-round best available arm and a single arm fixed over a block, showing that this gap is governed by the cumulative variation within the block. Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.4 Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> then combines this control with the one-step OMD bound to obtain a regret bound against a fixed comparator over the block. Together, these results allow the per-round inequalities to be aggregated while isolating the effect of non-stationarity.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a block <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}=\{t_{0},t_{0}+1,\dots,t_{0}+L-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}=\{t_{0},t_{0}+1,\dots,t_{0}+L-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Dentoe the blockwise best arm as</span></p>
<table id="A4.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\arg\min_{i\in[K]}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>arg</mi><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\arg\min_{i\in[K]}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,i}\mathbb{I}\{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be as defined in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Restatement of Theorem ) ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left(\widehat{L}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in C_{t}\}-\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}}\right)\leq L\sum_{t\in B\setminus\{t_{0}\}}\Delta_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left(\widehat{L}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in C_{t}\}-\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}}\right)\leq L\sum_{t\in B\setminus\{t_{0}\}}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}(C)=\min_{i\in C}\widehat{L}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}(C)=\min_{i\in C}\widehat{L}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Lipschitz property of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>min</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min</annotation></semantics></math>, it satisfies</p>
<table id="A4.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|b_{t}(C)-b_{t-1}(C)\right|\leq\max_{i\in C}\left|\widehat{L}_{t,i}-\widehat{L}_{t-1,i}\right|\leq\Delta_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|b_{t}(C)-b_{t-1}(C)\right|\leq\max_{i\in C}\left|\widehat{L}_{t,i}-\widehat{L}_{t-1,i}\right|\leq\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By telescoping (<a href="#A4.E56" title="Eq. 56 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.4 Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) from <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t_{0}}(C_{t})\leq b_{t}(C_{t})+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}=m_{t}+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t_{0}}(C_{t})\leq b_{t}(C_{t})+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}=m_{t}+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By definition of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the best static arm for the block</p>
<table id="A4.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{b_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}\leq\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}^{t_{0}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{t}^{t_{0}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{b_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}\leq\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}^{t_{0}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{t}^{t_{0}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Also note that by definition,</p>
<table id="A4.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}^{t_{0}}}\leq\widehat{L}_{t_{0},m_{t}^{t_{0}}}+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}=b_{t_{0}}(\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}^{t_{0}}}\leq\widehat{L}_{t_{0},m_{t}^{t_{0}}}+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}=b_{t_{0}}(\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t})+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Combine (<a href="#A4.E56" title="Eq. 56 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.4 Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E59" title="Eq. 59 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.4 Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A4.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}\leq\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left(\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}}+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}\leq\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left(\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}}+\sum_{\tau=t_{0}+1}^{t}\Delta_{\tau}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Rearranging, we get</p>
<table id="A4.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}-\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}}\leq L\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}\setminus\{t_{0}\}}\Delta_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\widehat{L}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}-\widehat{L}_{t,m_{t}}\leq L\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}\setminus\{t_{0}\}}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a block <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}=\{t_{0},t_{0}+1,\dots,t_{0}+L-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}=\{t_{0},t_{0}+1,\dots,t_{0}+L-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Run Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Idealized OSMD algorithm ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> starting from time <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{q}_{t}\in\Delta_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{q}_{t}\in\Delta_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the played distribution at each round <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be an unbiased estimator of the masked loss vector</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EE[\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}]=\boldsymbol{L}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐋</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\widehat{\boldsymbol{L}}_{t}\mid\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}]=\boldsymbol{L}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and that the second moment is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A4.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EE\left[\sum_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{q}_{t,i}\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{2}\right]\leq\frac{k}{s}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\left[\sum_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{q}_{t,i}\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{2}\right]\leq\frac{k}{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{C_{t}}\right\rangle-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}\right]\leq\frac{\log(1/\alpha)}{\eta}+\frac{sk\eta L}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sk</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE\left[\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{C_{t}}\right\rangle-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}\right]\leq\frac{\log(1/\alpha)}{\eta}+\frac{sk\eta L}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof:</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> and any comparators <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\in\Delta_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\in\Delta_{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, apply Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 ‣ D.3 One-Step OMD Bound ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></p>
<table id="A4.E64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}-\boldsymbol{v}_{t},\boldsymbol{L}_{t}\right\rangle\leq\frac{1}{\eta}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left(\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t+1})\right)+\frac{\eta s^{2}}{2}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\sum_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{q}_{t,i}\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}-\boldsymbol{v}_{t},\boldsymbol{L}_{t}\right\rangle\leq\frac{1}{\eta}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left(\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t+1})\right)+\frac{\eta s^{2}}{2}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\sum_{i\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\boldsymbol{q}_{t,i}\widehat{L}_{t,i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By the unbiasedness of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{y}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EE[\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}-\boldsymbol{v}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle]=\EE\left[\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}-\boldsymbol{v}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE[\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}-\boldsymbol{v}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}\right\rangle]=\EE\left[\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t}-\boldsymbol{v}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For the KL terms, we have</p>
<table id="A4.E65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.E65X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left(\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t+1})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left(\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t+1})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t_{0}})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t_{0}+L-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒒</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t_{0}})-\mathrm{KL}(\boldsymbol{v}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{q}_{t_{0}+L-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E65Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log(1/\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log(1/\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where the first equality is a result of telescoping with respect to <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and the second due to the fact that <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> is restarted from uniform.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the second term on the RHS of (<a href="#A4.E64" title="Eq. 64 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.4 Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>), we invoke Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Bounded Second Moment) ‣ Proof: ‣ D.2 Moment Lemmas ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Taking expectation on both sides, we get (<a href="#A4.E63" title="Eq. 63 ‣ Lemma 6 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.4 Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>).
 <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Restatement of Theorem ) ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that</p>
<table id="A4.E66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{t}}=\left(\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}\right)+\left(\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{t}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒍</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒍</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{t}}=\left(\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}\right)+\left(\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}}\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{\mathcal{B}}}\mathbb{I}\{m_{\mathcal{B}}\in\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}\}-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{t}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We bound the first term using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6 ‣ Proof: ‣ D.4 Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and the second term using <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 ‣ D.4 Reduction to Blockwise Fixed Arm ‣ Appendix D Regret Analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Taking the expectation and summing over blocks, we get</p>
<table id="A4.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Reg}_{n}^{\mathrm{BA}}=\EE\left[\sum_{i=1}^{B}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}_{i}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{t}}\right]\leq\frac{T}{L}\frac{\log(1/\alpha)}{\eta}+\frac{\eta sk}{2}T+LV_{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>BA</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐥</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐥</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sk</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>LV</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Reg}_{n}^{\mathrm{BA}}=\EE\left[\sum_{i=1}^{B}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}_{i}}\left\langle\boldsymbol{q}_{t},\boldsymbol{l}_{t}^{\tilde{\mathcal{X}}_{t}}\right\rangle-\boldsymbol{l}_{t,m_{t}}\right]\leq\frac{T}{L}\frac{\log(1/\alpha)}{\eta}+\frac{\eta sk}{2}T+LV_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Take</p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{T}{V_{n}}\sqrt{\frac{sk\log(1/\alpha)}{2}}\right)^{2/3}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{T}{V_{n}}\sqrt{\frac{sk\log(1/\alpha)}{2}}\right)^{2/3},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E69.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2^{2/3}\,(\log(1/\alpha))^{1/3}\,(sk)^{-2/3}\left(\frac{V_{n}}{T}\right)^{1/3}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2^{2/3}\,(\log(1/\alpha))^{1/3}\,(sk)^{-2/3}\left(\frac{V_{n}}{T}\right)^{1/3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">we get</p>
<table id="A4.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Reg}_{n}^{\mathrm{BA}}\;\leq\;\frac{3}{2^{1/3}}\,\big(T^{2}\,sk\,\log(1/\alpha)\,V_{n}\big)^{1/3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Reg</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>BA</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Reg}_{n}^{\mathrm{BA}}\;\leq\;\frac{3}{2^{1/3}}\,\big(T^{2}\,sk\,\log(1/\alpha)\,V_{n}\big)^{1/3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Performance improvement contribution of each problem</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide further justification for the per-problem policy improvement contribution
defined in <a href="#S3.E6" title="In Per-problem utility. ‣ 3.2 Policy improvement as the curator learning signal ‣ 3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Intuitively, this quantity measures the marginal
contribution of including a training problem <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math> in an actor update to the
overall improvement in policy performance under the evaluation distribution
<math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This interpretation is exact for a broad class of <em id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">tabular policies</em>, where the policy
parameters for different problems (or states) are independent. In such settings, updating
the policy using trajectories from a problem <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math> affects only the conditional
distribution <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math> and leaves the policy unchanged on all other
problems.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Example: tabular REINFORCE.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider tabular REINFORCE, where for each problem <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math> the policy
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is parameterized independently.
At iteration <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose we update the policy using rollouts collected <em id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">only</em> from a
single problem <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By construction, this update modifies <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math> but does not change
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime}\neq\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime}\neq\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The overall performance objective is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\pi)=\sum_{\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}}p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime})\,\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime})}\bigl[R(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime})\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi)=\sum_{\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}}p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime})\,\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime})}\bigl[R(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime})\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Since only the conditional policy at <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is changed, the performance difference
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{t+1})-J(\pi^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{t+1})-J(\pi^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> depends solely on how the expected reward at <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math>
changes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the standard performance difference identity
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kakade and Langford, 2002</a>)</cite> to the single-turn setting yields</p>
<table id="A5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\pi^{t+1})-J(\pi^{t})=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})}\left[\frac{\pi^{t+1}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}{\pi^{t}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}A_{\pi^{t}}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{t+1})-J(\pi^{t})=p_{\mathcal{X}}(\boldsymbol{x})\,\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{y}\sim\pi^{t}(\cdot\mid\boldsymbol{x})}\left[\frac{\pi^{t+1}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}{\pi^{t}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})}A_{\pi^{t}}(\boldsymbol{y}\mid\boldsymbol{x})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which is exactly the per-problem utility <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in
<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Per-problem utility. ‣ 3.2 Policy improvement as the curator learning signal ‣ 3 Method ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
Thus, in tabular REINFORCE, updating the policy on a single problem <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math>
produces an expected performance improvement of <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The same reasoning extends directly to batch updates: if the policy is updated using a
subset of problems <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total performance improvement decomposes additively
as <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}}u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}^{t}}u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and including a problem
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math> in the update contributes exactly <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> to the expected
performance gain.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Other tabular methods.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This exact additive interpretation applies equally to other tabular reinforcement learning
methods, including tabular policy gradient methods, tabular Q-learning, and SARSA, where
updates based on a problem or state affect only the corresponding local policy or value
parameters. In all such cases, the per-problem utility <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> captures the
true marginal contribution of training on <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion: function approximation.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the presence of function approximation, updating the policy using trajectories from one
problem generally affects the policy on other problems as well, breaking the exact
additivity described above. Analyzing such cross-problem interference requires strong
assumptions on the structure of the function class and the optimization dynamics, and is
beyond the scope of this work.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Nevertheless, when policy updates are small—as is typical in modern RL post-training
algorithms such as PPO-style methods, GRPO, or GSPO—the per-problem utility
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{t}_{\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> remains a first-order approximation to the marginal contribution of
problem <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math> to performance improvement. Our empirical results in
<a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Main results ‣ 4 Experimental results ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sec.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> indicate that this approximation is sufficiently accurate to drive
effective curriculum learning at scale.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Limitations</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While <span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Actor-Curator</span> is agnostic to the specific actor update rule and can be combined with a wide range of post-training algorithms, its gains ultimately depend on the stability and quality of the underlying actor optimization: unstable updates can still lead to noisy dynamics or training collapse, a common failure mode in reinforcement learning that curriculum learning alone cannot fully address. In addition, <span id="A6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Actor-Curator</span> inherits standard assumptions from RL-based LLM post-training, most notably access to a reliable reward signal, making it best suited to domains with objectively verifiable rewards such as mathematics, logic puzzles, and code. Finally, learning an explicit curator introduces additional computational overhead beyond standard RL post-training; while modest relative to actor training and rollout generation, this cost is non-negligible, and in our experiments <span id="A6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Actor-Curator</span> increases overall wall-clock training time by approximately 9% (see <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Additional analysis ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">App.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a>), though this overhead is small compared to the observed gains in training efficiency.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Experimental setup</h2>

<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Hyper-parameters</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise specified, all experiments use the same hyper-parameter configuration for <span id="A7.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Actor-Curator</span>. The complete set of hyper-parameters is summarized in Table <a href="#A7.T2" title="Tab. 2 ‣ G.1 Hyper-parameters ‣ Appendix G Experimental setup ‣ Actor-Curator: Co-adaptive Curriculum Learning via Policy-Improvement Bandits for Scalable RL Post-Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We briefly explain key parameters below, with a focus on those specific to the actor–curator framework.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T2" class="ltx_table">
